# What never reaches the build daemon.
#
# The first entry is the one that matters for more than speed. The Dockerfile
# copies named paths rather than `.`, so `.env` is not in the image today — but
# this is what keeps that true if a broad `COPY . .` is ever added, and SEC-01's
# "never commit .env" and "never ship .env" are the same concern one step apart.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# 101M of the 108M working tree, and none of it belongs in an image that installs
# its own dependencies. Sending it costs build time on every rebuild.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

.git/
.github/

# Runtime state. These are bind-mounted at run time from the host, so a copy in
# the image would be a stale shadow of the real thing — and the FIT archive is
# the one directory in the system that must never be duplicated or pruned
# (FIT-15).
var/
backups/

# Documentation and tests. Both are the reason this repository is reviewable and
# neither is needed to run it. Excluded rather than copied so the image stays
# small and `pip install` cannot pick up a test dependency.
docs/
tests/
*.md
!README.md
